 "how": "the finite mathematics of the package's six hand derivations, rebuilt on main along the discriminators its own review brief asks for (checks/physical_four_form.py; nothing of the lane's run). THE QUOTIENT: Z = P R^t has determinant 0, a rank-one matrix has a balanced representative unique up to the circle, and the potential is |P|^2 + |R|^2 there. THE CONNECTION: the Gauss field is [Im(P^dagger dP) - Im(R^dagger dR)]/N and the metric |dP|^2 + |dR|^2 - J^2/N (by direct minimisation; a plus sign on the negative charge gives another answer; a phase change shifts it by d phi). THE PRIMITIVE PERIOD: on v = conj(u) the connection is the Hopf one, with period 1; one Hopf term alone gives 1/2; the latitude's holonomy is exp(-i pi (1 - cos theta0)). THE CENTRE: on E8 the charges are in thirds, so exp(2 pi i Q) has order 3 and is 1 on the four singlets, and the effective circle's first Chern number is three times the full circle's: the primitive bundle does not lift through the pure charge circle, and does lift with colour carried (det E = L^-1; the transition diag(exp(i x), exp(-i x), 1, 1) closes). THE NORMALISATION: the reduced symplectic potential t^2 (a_u + a_v) vanishes on the primitive sphere and the connection does not change when the action is scaled. THE DIRECT PAIR MAP: on one gauge orbit the commutator trace of the pair runs from -2 to 2 (2 - 4 cos^2 phi), so it does not descend; with a reference phase carried the pair is invariant; a reference of weight nu^2 adds N nu^2/(N + nu^2)(dchi - A)^2; no global reference exists over the primitive sphere; the shear has no invariant positive metric at the trivial pair and preserves |Y - tau X|^2/Im tau with tau moved. THE COMPOSITE: A = U J U^-1, W = U U(conj v)^-1 is invariant and lossless; the quotient metric is (t^2/2)(|DA|^2 + |k|^2) and the connection a_u - <A, k>/2 (finite differences on a random curve, eight digits); tr[A, W] = 2 - 4(|w|^2 - (n.w)^2), equal to 2 on the whole primitive sphere; v -> i v is the shear, of order 4. THE RADIAL CHART: its metric change is the note's. THE CONSTRAINED PHASE: the least extra energy is Delta^2/int dx/N, and two intervals sew with their integrals added",
